{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ECC",
  "chapter": 10,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Dead flies cause the ointment of the apothecary to send forth an offensive odor: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so doth",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a little folly him that is in reputation for wisdom ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " honor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A wise man's heart ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " at his right hand; but a fool's heart ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " at his left.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also, when he that is a fool walketh by the way, his wisdom faileth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and he saith to every one ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a fool.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If the spirit of the ruler riseth against thee, leave not thy place; for yielding pacifieth great offenses.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is an evil ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I have seen under the sun, as an error ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " proceedeth from the ruler:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Folly is set in great dignity, and the rich sit in low place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have seen servants upon horses, and princes walking as servants upon the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that diggeth a pit shall fall into it; and whoever breaketh a hedge, a serpent shall bite him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whoever removeth stones shall be hurt by them; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he that cleaveth wood shall be endangered by it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If the iron is blunt, and he doth not whet the edge, then must he use more strength: but wisdom ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " profitable to direct.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Surely the serpent will bite without enchantment; and a babbler is no better.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The words of a wise man's mouth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " gracious; but the lips of a fool will swallow up himself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The beginning of the words of his mouth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " foolishness: and the end of his talk ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mischievous madness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A fool also is full of words: a man cannot tell what shall be; and what shall be after him, who can tell him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The labor of the foolish wearieth every one of them, because he knoweth not how to go to the city.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Woe to thee, O land, when thy king ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a child, and thy princes eat in the morning!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Blessed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou, O land, when thy king ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the son of nobles, and thy princes eat in due season, for strength, and not for drunkenness!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "By much slothfulness the building decayeth; and through idleness of the hands the house droppeth through.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A feast is made for laughter, and wine maketh merry: but money answereth all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.10.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.10.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Curse not the king, no not in thy thought; and curse not the rich in thy bed-chamber: for a bird of the air will carry the voice, and that which hath wings will tell the matter.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
